IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `maib-core`
IMPORT `maib-seat`

-- Cases for the individual's seat (maib-seat.l4): the injured person, and the dependants, personal representative and
-- family members after a death. Every case is HYPOTHETICAL: no scenario life raised this Act.
--
-- Every expected value was worked by hand from the deposited Act (act-1973-071.txt) and Regulations (sr-2020-007.txt),
-- with the arithmetic in the comment above the assertion. The calendar dates were then checked independently with
-- Python's datetime, not against the encoding. Adult average weekly earnings figures are made up for the tests (the
-- ABS series is an input, not deposited).
--
-- The accident in most cases: Tuesday 10 March 2026.

`the accident` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 10 3 2026

§ `Cases -- the injured person and the family`

§§ `Daily care (s 2 (5), s 27A)`

-- 2 hours a day, indefinitely, from within a year: s 2 (5) is met.
#ASSERT `Do I require daily care` 2 TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE
-- 1.5 hours a day: below the 2 hours.
#ASSERT NOT (`Do I require daily care` 1.5 TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE)
-- 6 hours a day, but starting more than a year after the accident: not met.
#ASSERT NOT (`Do I require daily care` 6 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- 6 hours a day for a fixed period (not indefinite): not met.
#ASSERT NOT (`Do I require daily care` 6 FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE)
-- s 27A (3): an accepted offer made on the basis of daily care: taken to require it.
#ASSERT `Do I require daily care` 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE
-- s 27A (2) (a): a court's certificate.
#ASSERT `Do I require daily care` 0 FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE

§§ `Liability (ss 2B, 23, 24)`

-- A case with no exclusion: the person was a passenger or pedestrian (owned and drove nothing), and nobody was
-- convicted. Daily care: the given hours, indefinitely, from within a year.
GIVEN `where`      IS A `Place`
      `lives`      IS A `Place`
      `tas`        IS A `How the injury resulted from the vehicle`
      `inter`      IS A `How the injury resulted from the vehicle`
      `other`      IS A `How the injury resulted from the vehicle`
      `care hours` IS A NUMBER
      `reported`   IS A BOOLEAN
      `excused`    IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `The Board's liability`
`a passenger's case` `where` `lives` `tas` `inter` `other` `care hours` `reported` `excused` MEANS
    `Is MAIB liable to pay me scheduled benefits for this accident` `where` `lives` `tas` `inter` `other`
        `care hours` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE
        `reported` `excused`
        FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
        FALSE FALSE FALSE `any other motor vehicle` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
        `none of the offences in s 24 (2) (a)` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE

-- L1. s 23 (1) (a): a Tasmanian resident hit in Hobart by an unregistered car. (1) (a) needs no registered vehicle.
`L1` MEANS `a passenger's case` `in this State` `in this State` `none of those` `none of those` `a collision, or action taken to avoid a collision, with it` 0 TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `L1`'s `for medical benefits` EQUALS `payable`
#ASSERT `L1`'s `for funeral benefits` EQUALS `payable`
#ASSERT `L1`'s `for death benefits` EQUALS `payable`
#ASSERT `L1`'s `for disability allowances` EQUALS `payable`
#ASSERT `L1`'s `for disability benefits` EQUALS `payable`
#ASSERT `L1`'s `for counselling services benefits` EQUALS `payable`

-- L2. s 23 (1) (b), (1AA): a Tasmanian resident injured in Victoria as a passenger in a Tasmanian-registered car.
-- Payable, less what Victorian law pays.
`L2` MEANS `a passenger's case` `in another State or a Territory` `in this State` `the driving of it` `none of those` `none of those` 0 TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `L2`'s `for medical benefits` EQUALS `payable less the benefits payable under the law of the other State or Territory (s 23 (1AA))`
#ASSERT `L2`'s `for disability allowances` EQUALS `payable less the benefits payable under the law of the other State or Territory (s 23 (1AA))`
#ASSERT `L2`'s `for death benefits` EQUALS `payable less the benefits payable under the law of the other State or Territory (s 23 (1AA))`

-- L3. A Tasmanian resident injured in New South Wales, only interstate vehicles involved: (1) (b) needs a vehicle
-- registered in this State.
`L3` MEANS `a passenger's case` `in another State or a Territory` `in this State` `none of those` `a collision, or action taken to avoid a collision, with it` `none of those` 0 TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `L3`'s `for medical benefits` EQUALS `not payable` `none of s 23 (1), (1A) and (2) applies`
#ASSERT `L3`'s `for funeral benefits` EQUALS `not payable` `none of s 23 (1), (1A) and (2) applies`

-- L4. s 23 (1A): a Victorian resident walking in Launceston, struck by a Tasmanian-registered car.
`L4` MEANS `a passenger's case` `in this State` `in another State or a Territory` `a collision, or action taken to avoid a collision, with it` `none of those` `none of those` 0 TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `L4`'s `for medical benefits` EQUALS `payable`
#ASSERT `L4`'s `for disability allowances` EQUALS `payable`
#ASSERT `L4`'s `for death benefits` EQUALS `payable`

-- L5. s 23 (1A) reaches a visitor from overseas too: "a person who is not a resident of this State".
`L5` MEANS `a passenger's case` `in this State` `outside the Commonwealth` `it moving out of control` `none of those` `none of those` 0 TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `L5`'s `for medical benefits` EQUALS `payable`
#ASSERT `L5`'s `for counselling services benefits` EQUALS `payable`

-- L5a. The same visitor, hit in Tasmania by an unregistered car (no Tasmanian-registered vehicle): (1A) is not met,
-- though a Tasmanian resident in the same accident is covered by (1) (a) (L1; finding 1).
`L5a` MEANS `a passenger's case` `in this State` `outside the Commonwealth` `none of those` `none of those` `a collision, or action taken to avoid a collision, with it` 0 TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `L5a`'s `for medical benefits` EQUALS `not payable` `none of s 23 (1), (1A) and (2) applies`

-- L6. s 23 (2): a Victorian resident, injured in Tasmania when their own Victorian car ran off the road (no
-- Tasmanian-registered vehicle involved), needs 6 hours' daily care indefinitely. Only medical benefits, disability
-- benefits and counselling benefits for family members. They owned and drove it; the Victorian premium was paid, so
-- (ga) does not apply; and on the encoding's reading (finding 4) (g) does not either, though no Tasmanian premium was
-- ever paid for the car.
`L6` MEANS
    `Is MAIB liable to pay me scheduled benefits for this accident` `in this State` `in another State or a Territory`
        `none of those` `it moving out of control` `none of those`
        6 TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE
        TRUE FALSE
        FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
        TRUE TRUE TRUE `any other motor vehicle` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE
        `none of the offences in s 24 (2) (a)` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `L6`'s `for medical benefits` EQUALS `payable`
#ASSERT `L6`'s `for disability benefits` EQUALS `payable`
#ASSERT `L6`'s `for counselling services benefits` EQUALS `payable`
#ASSERT `L6`'s `for disability allowances` EQUALS `not payable` `s 23 (2) covers only medical benefits, disability benefits and counselling benefits for family members`
#ASSERT `L6`'s `for funeral benefits` EQUALS `not payable` `s 23 (2) covers only medical benefits, disability benefits and counselling benefits for family members`
#ASSERT `L6`'s `for death benefits` EQUALS `not payable` `s 23 (2) covers only medical benefits, disability benefits and counselling benefits for family members`

-- L7. The same accident, but the Victorian needs only 1 hour's care a day: s 23 (2) (c) is not met.
`L7` MEANS `a passenger's case` `in this State` `in another State or a Territory` `none of those` `it moving out of control` `none of those` 1 TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `L7`'s `for medical benefits` EQUALS `not payable` `none of s 23 (1), (1A) and (2) applies`

-- L8. s 23 (2A): a Tasmanian resident injured in Tasmania; the accident was not reported to police as soon as
-- practicable. Nothing, unless the Board excuses it.
`L8` MEANS `a passenger's case` `in this State` `in this State` `the driving of it` `none of those` `none of those` 0 FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `L8`'s `for medical benefits` EQUALS `not payable` `the accident was not reported to a police officer as soon as practicable, and the Board has not excused the failure (s 23 (2A))`
#ASSERT `L8`'s `for counselling services benefits` EQUALS `not payable` `the accident was not reported to a police officer as soon as practicable, and the Board has not excused the failure (s 23 (2A))`
`L8 excused` MEANS `a passenger's case` `in this State` `in this State` `the driving of it` `none of those` `none of those` 0 FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT `L8 excused`'s `for medical benefits` EQUALS `payable`

-- L9. s 2 (4): a fall on a stationary bus's step, no collision, no loss of control, not caused by its driving.
`L9` MEANS `a passenger's case` `in this State` `in this State` `none of those` `none of those` `none of those` 0 TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `L9`'s `for medical benefits` EQUALS `not payable` `the personal injury does not result directly from a motor accident (s 2 (4))`

-- An own-vehicle case: a Tasmanian resident, in Tasmania, reported; the vehicle facts vary.
GIVEN `owned`       IS A BOOLEAN
      `drove`       IS A BOOLEAN
      `kind`        IS A `Kind of vehicle`
      `premium paid` IS A BOOLEAN
      `knew`        IS A BOOLEAN
      `permitted and insured` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `The Board's liability`
`a Tasmanian's own-vehicle case` `owned` `drove` `kind` `premium paid` `knew` `permitted and insured` MEANS
    `Is MAIB liable to pay me scheduled benefits for this accident` `in this State` `in this State`
        `none of those` `none of those` `it moving out of control`
        0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
        TRUE FALSE
        FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
        `owned` `drove` TRUE `kind` FALSE `premium paid` FALSE FALSE `knew` `permitted and insured`
        `none of the offences in s 24 (2) (a)` `drove` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE

-- L10. s 24 (1) (g): the owner-driver of an unregistered car (no premium paid) that ran off the road.
`L10` MEANS `a Tasmanian's own-vehicle case` TRUE TRUE `any other motor vehicle` FALSE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `L10`'s `for medical benefits` EQUALS `not payable` (`excluded by s 24 (1)` `(g) no premium was paid, and the person was the owner, or a driver who knew or ought to have known`)
#ASSERT `L10`'s `for death benefits` EQUALS `not payable` (`excluded by s 24 (1)` `(g) no premium was paid, and the person was the owner, or a driver who knew or ought to have known`)

-- L11. (g) (ii) (A): a driver (not the owner) who neither knew nor ought to have known the premium was unpaid.
`L11` MEANS `a Tasmanian's own-vehicle case` FALSE TRUE `any other motor vehicle` FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `L11`'s `for medical benefits` EQUALS `payable`

-- L12. s 24 (1A): the Tasmanian owner-driver of a permitted out-of-State vehicle with a third party policy in force.
`L12` MEANS `a Tasmanian's own-vehicle case` TRUE TRUE `any other motor vehicle` FALSE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT `L12`'s `for medical benefits` EQUALS `payable`

-- L13. s 24 (1) (e): the owner riding an unregistered farm bike (no premium). (e) comes before (g) in the text.
`L13` MEANS `a Tasmanian's own-vehicle case` TRUE TRUE `a trail bike, farm bike or beach buggy` FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `L13`'s `for disability allowances` EQUALS `not payable` (`excluded by s 24 (1)` `(e) the person owned or drove a trail bike, farm bike or beach buggy with no premium paid`)

-- L13a. (g) excepts a prescribed trailer (reg 11 (2)): the owner of an unregistered small box trailer whose use (it
-- came loose) caused the accident.
`L13a` MEANS `a Tasmanian's own-vehicle case` TRUE FALSE `a trailer of a kind prescribed by reg 11 (2)` FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `L13a`'s `for medical benefits` EQUALS `payable`

-- L14. s 24 (1) (ea): a Victorian resident riding their own Victorian trail bike in Tasmania, Victorian premium
-- required but unpaid, hit by a Tasmanian-registered car (so s 23 (1A) applies).
`L14` MEANS
    `Is MAIB liable to pay me scheduled benefits for this accident` `in this State` `in another State or a Territory`
        `a collision, or action taken to avoid a collision, with it` `the driving of it` `none of those`
        0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
        TRUE FALSE
        FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
        TRUE TRUE TRUE `a trail bike, farm bike or beach buggy` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
        `none of the offences in s 24 (2) (a)` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `L14`'s `for medical benefits` EQUALS `not payable` (`excluded by s 24 (1)` `(ea) an interstate resident owned or drove an interstate trail bike, farm bike or beach buggy with no interstate premium paid`)

-- An exclusion case for s 24 (1) (a)-(d), (f), (h): a passenger, reported.
GIVEN `where` IS A `Place`
      `tas`   IS A `How the injury resulted from the vehicle`
      `a`     IS A BOOLEAN
      `b`     IS A BOOLEAN
      `ba`    IS A BOOLEAN
      `bb`    IS A BOOLEAN
      `c`     IS A BOOLEAN
      `d`     IS A BOOLEAN
      `f`     IS A BOOLEAN
      `h`     IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `The Board's liability`
`a s 24 (1) case` `where` `tas` `a` `b` `ba` `bb` `c` `d` `f` `h` MEANS
    `Is MAIB liable to pay me scheduled benefits for this accident` `where` `in this State`
        `tas` `none of those` `none of those`
        0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
        TRUE FALSE
        `a` `b` `ba` `bb` `c` `d` `f` `h`
        FALSE FALSE FALSE `any other motor vehicle` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
        `none of the offences in s 24 (2) (a)` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE

-- L15. s 24 (1) (ba) against s 23 (1AA): a Tasmanian injured in Victoria in a Tasmanian car, with Victorian motor
-- accident compensation payable. s 24 applies "notwithstanding section 23": nothing, so (1AA) never nets anything
-- off (finding 3).
`L15` MEANS `a s 24 (1) case` `in another State or a Territory` `the driving of it` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `L15`'s `for medical benefits` EQUALS `not payable` (`excluded by s 24 (1)` `(ba) compensation is payable for the injury under another Australian motor accidents compensation law`)

-- L16. s 24 (1) (b): workers compensation is payable (a work journey or a work vehicle).
`L16` MEANS `a s 24 (1) case` `in this State` `the driving of it` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `L16`'s `for funeral benefits` EQUALS `not payable` (`excluded by s 24 (1)` `(b) workers compensation is payable for the injury`)

-- L17. s 24 (1) (d): taking part in a motor vehicle race.
`L17` MEANS `a s 24 (1) case` `in this State` `the driving of it` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `L17`'s `for medical benefits` EQUALS `not payable` (`excluded by s 24 (1)` `(d) a motor accident in a motor vehicle race in which the person was taking part`)

-- L18. s 24 (1) (a) and (h) together: the first in the text is reported.
`L18` MEANS `a s 24 (1) case` `in this State` `the driving of it` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT `L18`'s `for medical benefits` EQUALS `not payable` (`excluded by s 24 (1)` `(a) the injury results from the person intentionally causing or attempting to cause personal injury`)

-- A driving case: a Tasmanian resident driving a Tasmanian-registered car (premium paid) in Tasmania, reported.
GIVEN `conviction` IS A `Section 24 (2) (a) conviction`
      `licensed`   IS A BOOLEAN
      `exempt`     IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 24 (3)`   IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 24 (3A)`  IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `The Board's liability`
`a driver's case` `conviction` `licensed` `exempt` `s 24 (3)` `s 24 (3A)` MEANS
    `Is MAIB liable to pay me scheduled benefits for this accident` `in this State` `in this State`
        `the driving of it` `none of those` `none of those`
        0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
        TRUE FALSE
        FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
        TRUE TRUE TRUE `any other motor vehicle` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
        `conviction` TRUE `licensed` `exempt` `s 24 (3)` `s 24 (3A)`

-- L19. s 24 (2) (a): convicted of dangerous driving. No medical benefit, disability benefit or disability allowance;
-- the others (funeral, death, counselling) are untouched.
`L19` MEANS `a driver's case` `dangerous driving` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `L19`'s `for medical benefits` EQUALS `not payable` `excluded by s 24 (2) (a): a conviction arising out of the person's driving at the time of the accident`
#ASSERT `L19`'s `for disability allowances` EQUALS `not payable` `excluded by s 24 (2) (a): a conviction arising out of the person's driving at the time of the accident`
#ASSERT `L19`'s `for disability benefits` EQUALS `not payable` `excluded by s 24 (2) (a): a conviction arising out of the person's driving at the time of the accident`
#ASSERT `L19`'s `for funeral benefits` EQUALS `payable`
#ASSERT `L19`'s `for death benefits` EQUALS `payable`
#ASSERT `L19`'s `for counselling services benefits` EQUALS `payable`

-- L20. s 24 (2) (b): driving with no licence of the class, not exempt.
`L20` MEANS `a driver's case` `none of the offences in s 24 (2) (a)` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `L20`'s `for medical benefits` EQUALS `not payable` `excluded by s 24 (2) (b): driving without a driver licence of the relevant class, exemption or authority`
#ASSERT `L20`'s `for death benefits` EQUALS `payable`
-- L21. s 24 (3): the licence lapsed by inadvertence and could be renewed.
`L21` MEANS `a driver's case` `none of the offences in s 24 (2) (a)` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `L21`'s `for medical benefits` EQUALS `payable`
-- L22. s 24 (3A): suspended only for unpaid fines.
`L22` MEANS `a driver's case` `none of the offences in s 24 (2) (a)` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT `L22`'s `for disability allowances` EQUALS `payable`
-- L23. A licensed driver convicted of nothing: everything payable.
`L23` MEANS `a driver's case` `none of the offences in s 24 (2) (a)` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `L23`'s `for disability allowances` EQUALS `payable`

§§ `Claiming (s 23 (2A), reg 10, s 28, s 26)`

-- Accident 10 March 2026; loss incurred 1 June 2026. reg 10 (2): notice by 10 March 2027; claim by 1 June 2027.
`C1` MEANS `What must I do to claim, and by when` `the accident` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 6 2026) FALSE FALSE `the accident` FALSE `the accident`
#ASSERT `C1`'s `report to a police officer` EQUALS `report the accident to a police officer as soon as practicable, or the Board must excuse the failure (s 23 (2A))`
#ASSERT `C1`'s `give the Board written notice of the injury by` EQUALS DATE_FROM_DMY 10 3 2027
#ASSERT `C1`'s `bring the claim by` EQUALS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 6 2027
-- Reported already.
#ASSERT (`What must I do to claim, and by when` `the accident` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 6 2026) TRUE FALSE `the accident` FALSE `the accident`)'s `report to a police officer` EQUALS `reported: nothing more to do`
-- An accident on 29 February 2028: one year later is read as 28 February 2029.
#ASSERT (`What must I do to claim, and by when` (DATE_FROM_DMY 29 2 2028) (DATE_FROM_DMY 29 2 2028) TRUE FALSE `the accident` FALSE `the accident`)'s `give the Board written notice of the injury by` EQUALS DATE_FROM_DMY 28 2 2029
-- reg 10 (3): the Tribunal extends the notice period to 1 September 2027.
#ASSERT (`What must I do to claim, and by when` `the accident` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 6 2026) TRUE TRUE (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 2027) FALSE `the accident`)'s `give the Board written notice of the injury by` EQUALS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 2027
-- An extension to 1 January 2033 is more than 5 years past 10 March 2027: cut to 10 March 2032.
#ASSERT (`What must I do to claim, and by when` `the accident` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 6 2026) TRUE TRUE (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2033) FALSE `the accident`)'s `give the Board written notice of the injury by` EQUALS DATE_FROM_DMY 10 3 2032

-- In time: notice on the last day, the claim on the last day.
#ASSERT `Is my claim in time` `the accident` (DATE_FROM_DMY 10 3 2027) (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 6 2026) (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 6 2027) FALSE `the accident` FALSE `the accident` EQUALS `in time`
-- Notice one day late.
#ASSERT `Is my claim in time` `the accident` (DATE_FROM_DMY 11 3 2027) (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 6 2026) (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 6 2027) FALSE `the accident` FALSE `the accident` EQUALS `out of time: written notice of the injury was not given within the period (reg 10 (2) (a))`
-- The claim one day late.
#ASSERT `Is my claim in time` `the accident` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 4 2026) (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 6 2026) (DATE_FROM_DMY 2 6 2027) FALSE `the accident` FALSE `the accident` EQUALS `out of time: the claim was not brought within the period (reg 10 (2) (b))`
-- reg 10 (4): notice given on 1 August 2027, after the year, but the Tribunal later extended the period to 1 September
-- 2027.
#ASSERT `Is my claim in time` `the accident` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 8 2027) (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 6 2026) (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 8 2027) TRUE (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 2027) TRUE (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 2027) EQUALS `in time`
-- A death claim: death on 20 March 2026; claim by 20 March 2027. Brought 21 March 2027: late.
#ASSERT `Is my claim in time` `the accident` (DATE_FROM_DMY 15 3 2026) (DATE_FROM_DMY 20 3 2026) (DATE_FROM_DMY 21 3 2027) FALSE `the accident` FALSE `the accident` EQUALS `out of time: the claim was not brought within the period (reg 10 (2) (b))`

-- s 28 (2).
#ASSERT `Can I take MAIB's decision to the Tribunal` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `Can I take MAIB's decision to the Tribunal` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Can I take MAIB's decision to the Tribunal` FALSE FALSE)

-- s 26: the 2020 Regulations make no provision, so an Age Pension changes nothing.
#ASSERT NOT (`Does my Commonwealth pension reduce my MAIB benefits` TRUE)

§§ `Medical benefits and the cap (Sch 1 Pt 1 cl 8, Pt 2)`

-- cl 8 (b): no daily care, 4 days in hospital (not "more than 4"): $400 000.
#ASSERT `What cap applies to my medical and disability benefits` `the accident` 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 4 EQUALS `capped at` 400000
-- cl 8 (a): 5 continuous days: $500 000.
#ASSERT `What cap applies to my medical and disability benefits` `the accident` 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 5 EQUALS `capped at` 500000
-- Daily care (8 hours, indefinitely, from within a year): no cap.
#ASSERT `What cap applies to my medical and disability benefits` `the accident` 8 TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE 30 EQUALS `no cap, because the person requires daily care`
-- An accident on 1 May 2019, no daily care: the 2010 Regulations' cap applies: not covered.
#ASSERT `What cap applies to my medical and disability benefits` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 5 2019) 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 EQUALS `cap not covered` `an accident before 17 February 2020: the 2010 or 2000 Regulations apply, which are not deposited`
-- The same 2019 accident with daily care: the Act itself (s 23 (4) (a), (e)) excepts it from any cap.
#ASSERT `What cap applies to my medical and disability benefits` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 5 2019) 3 TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 EQUALS `no cap, because the person requires daily care`

-- $390 000 already paid under a $400 000 cap; a new $15 000 bill: $10 000 more.
#ASSERT `How much more can MAIB pay under the cap` `the accident` FALSE 0 390000 15000 EQUALS `dollars` 10000
-- Already over the cap: nothing more.
#ASSERT `How much more can MAIB pay under the cap` `the accident` FALSE 0 410000 15000 EQUALS `dollars` 0
-- Daily care: the whole $15 000.
#ASSERT `How much more can MAIB pay under the cap` `the accident` TRUE 0 410000 15000 EQUALS `dollars` 15000

-- Physiotherapy: $120 charged, $100 the most economical practicable cost, no Medicare: $100 (cl 1 (4) (a)).
#ASSERT `How much of this expense will MAIB pay as medical benefits` `the accident` `other treatment` 120 100 TRUE TRUE 0 FALSE 0 `the accident` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `dollars` 100
-- A GP visit of $80 with a $41.20 Medicare benefit: $38.80 (cl 1 (2)).
#ASSERT `How much of this expense will MAIB pay as medical benefits` `the accident` `other treatment` 80 80 TRUE TRUE 41.2 FALSE 0 `the accident` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `dollars` 38.8
-- Treatment that is not curative of the injury: unnecessarily incurred (cl 1 (4) (b); finding 9).
#ASSERT `How much of this expense will MAIB pay as medical benefits` `the accident` `other treatment` 80 80 FALSE TRUE 0 FALSE 0 `the accident` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `nothing payable` `unnecessarily incurred: the treatment is not warranted, beneficial and curative (Sch 1 Pt 2 cl 1 (4) (b))`
-- Treatment in New Zealand.
#ASSERT `How much of this expense will MAIB pay as medical benefits` `the accident` `other treatment` 500 500 TRUE FALSE 0 FALSE 0 `the accident` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `nothing payable` `not treatment required within the Commonwealth (Sch 1 Pt 2 cl 1 (1))`
-- A $30 taxi, 12 km, to an approved provider, certified, on 8 December 2026: the last day of the 39 weeks after
-- 10 March 2026 (10 March + 273 days). cl 1 (3) (j): $30.
#ASSERT `How much of this expense will MAIB pay as medical benefits` `the accident` `travel by taxi to obtain treatment` 30 30 TRUE TRUE 0 TRUE 12 (DATE_FROM_DMY 8 12 2026) TRUE FALSE EQUALS `dollars` 30
-- The same taxi on 9 December 2026: outside the 39 weeks, 20 km or less, no daily care: neither (j) nor (k).
#ASSERT `How much of this expense will MAIB pay as medical benefits` `the accident` `travel by taxi to obtain treatment` 30 30 TRUE TRUE 0 TRUE 12 (DATE_FROM_DMY 9 12 2026) TRUE FALSE EQUALS `nothing payable` `travel that meets neither Sch 1 Pt 2 cl 1 (3) (j) nor (k)`
-- ... but for a person requiring daily care, (k) (i): $30.
#ASSERT `How much of this expense will MAIB pay as medical benefits` `the accident` `travel by taxi to obtain treatment` 30 30 TRUE TRUE 0 TRUE 12 (DATE_FROM_DMY 9 12 2026) TRUE TRUE EQUALS `dollars` 30
-- An uncertified 12 km taxi: not (j).
#ASSERT `How much of this expense will MAIB pay as medical benefits` `the accident` `travel by taxi to obtain treatment` 30 30 TRUE TRUE 0 TRUE 12 (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 5 2026) FALSE FALSE EQUALS `nothing payable` `travel that meets neither Sch 1 Pt 2 cl 1 (3) (j) nor (k)`
