#ASSERT (`Which disability allowances could apply to me` FALSE FALSE TRUE 30 TRUE FALSE FALSE)'s `an employed person's allowance may apply`
-- ... with only 25 weeks: no.
#ASSERT NOT ((`Which disability allowances could apply to me` FALSE FALSE TRUE 25 TRUE FALSE FALSE)'s `an employed person's allowance may apply`)
-- cl 3 (2) (b): on the way from home to start work.
#ASSERT (`Which disability allowances could apply to me` FALSE TRUE TRUE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE)'s `an employed person's allowance may apply`

-- cl 7 (1) (a): $73 000 over the 365 days from 10 March 2025 to 9 March 2026: 73 000 / (365 / 7) = $1 400 a week.
#ASSERT `What are my average weekly earnings` `the accident` `continuously for the whole 12 months before the day of the accident` 73000 `the accident` 0 0 EQUALS 1400
-- cl 7 (1) (b): $39 000 since 9 September 2025, 182 days (26 weeks): $1 500 a week.
#ASSERT `What are my average weekly earnings` `the accident` `continuously, for one week or more but less than 12 months, up to the day of the accident` 39000 (DATE_FROM_DMY 9 9 2025) 0 0 EQUALS 1500
-- cl 7 (1) (c): started 3 days before; a comparable worker earns $1 100.
#ASSERT `What are my average weekly earnings` `the accident` `for less than one week before the accident` 0 `the accident` 1100 0 EQUALS 1100
-- cl 7 (1) (e): a job seeker with $24 000 over 30 weeks of earnings: $800.
#ASSERT `What are my average weekly earnings` `the accident` `not working at the time, but a job seeker under cl 3 (2) (c)` 24000 `the accident` 0 30 EQUALS 800

-- An employee in work for the whole year; adult AWE $2 000 (3 times: $6 000); wholly disabled from day 1.
GIVEN `how`        IS A `How I was working before the accident`
      `earnings`   IS A NUMBER
      `began`      IS A DATE
      `comparable` IS A NUMBER
      `this week`  IS A NUMBER
      `disabled`   IS A BOOLEAN
      `conviction` IS A `My alcohol or drug driving conviction`
      `level`      IS A NUMBER
      `satisfied`  IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `Allowance answer`
`an employee's allowance` `how` `earnings` `began` `comparable` `this week` `disabled` `conviction` `level` `satisfied` MEANS
    `What is my employed person's allowance` `the accident` TRUE FALSE TRUE 52 FALSE
        `how` `earnings` `began` `comparable` 0
        2000 `disabled` `this week` `conviction` `level` `satisfied`

-- AWE $1 400 (cl 7 (1) (a)): over $400, so the lesser of 80% ($1 120) and $6 000: $1 120 a week, from 17 March 2026
-- (cl 6 (1) (a): not the 7 days 10-16 March); first period to 6 March 2028 (10 March 2026 + 727 days, the last day
-- of 104 weeks); prescribed period to 3 March 2031 (+ 1 819 days, the last of 260 weeks).
#ASSERT `an employee's allowance` `continuously for the whole 12 months before the day of the accident` 73000 `the accident` 0 0 TRUE `none` 0 FALSE EQUALS `weekly allowance` `an employed person's allowance` 1120 1120 (DATE_FROM_DMY 17 3 2026) (DATE_FROM_DMY 6 3 2028) (DATE_FROM_DMY 3 3 2031)
-- cl 3 (7): $400 earned in a week of light duties: $1 120 - $400 = $720 that week.
#ASSERT `an employee's allowance` `continuously for the whole 12 months before the day of the accident` 73000 `the accident` 0 400 TRUE `none` 0 FALSE EQUALS `weekly allowance` `an employed person's allowance` 1120 720 (DATE_FROM_DMY 17 3 2026) (DATE_FROM_DMY 6 3 2028) (DATE_FROM_DMY 3 3 2031)
-- cl 3 (7) (b): $1 200 earned exceeds the allowance: nothing that week.
#ASSERT `an employee's allowance` `continuously for the whole 12 months before the day of the accident` 73000 `the accident` 0 1200 TRUE `none` 0 FALSE EQUALS `weekly allowance` `an employed person's allowance` 1120 0 (DATE_FROM_DMY 17 3 2026) (DATE_FROM_DMY 6 3 2028) (DATE_FROM_DMY 3 3 2031)
-- AWE $1 500 (cl 7 (1) (b)): 80% = $1 200. s 24 (4): s 6 (1) conviction at 0.08: two thirds, $800.
#ASSERT `an employee's allowance` `continuously, for one week or more but less than 12 months, up to the day of the accident` 39000 (DATE_FROM_DMY 9 9 2025) 0 0 TRUE `section 6 (1): driving with a prescribed concentration of alcohol` 0.08 FALSE EQUALS `weekly allowance` `an employed person's allowance` 800 800 (DATE_FROM_DMY 17 3 2026) (DATE_FROM_DMY 6 3 2028) (DATE_FROM_DMY 3 3 2031)
-- ... and $300 earned that week: cl 3 (7) first, then s 24 (4): (1 200 - 300) x 2/3 = $600 (a reading, finding 16).
#ASSERT `an employee's allowance` `continuously, for one week or more but less than 12 months, up to the day of the accident` 39000 (DATE_FROM_DMY 9 9 2025) 0 300 TRUE `section 6 (1): driving with a prescribed concentration of alcohol` 0.08 FALSE EQUALS `weekly allowance` `an employed person's allowance` 800 600 (DATE_FROM_DMY 17 3 2026) (DATE_FROM_DMY 6 3 2028) (DATE_FROM_DMY 3 3 2031)
-- ... at 0.15: one third, $400.
#ASSERT `an employee's allowance` `continuously, for one week or more but less than 12 months, up to the day of the accident` 39000 (DATE_FROM_DMY 9 9 2025) 0 0 TRUE `section 6 (1): driving with a prescribed concentration of alcohol` 0.15 FALSE EQUALS `weekly allowance` `an employed person's allowance` 400 400 (DATE_FROM_DMY 17 3 2026) (DATE_FROM_DMY 6 3 2028) (DATE_FROM_DMY 3 3 2031)
-- ... at 0.24: nil.
#ASSERT `an employee's allowance` `continuously, for one week or more but less than 12 months, up to the day of the accident` 39000 (DATE_FROM_DMY 9 9 2025) 0 0 TRUE `section 6 (1): driving with a prescribed concentration of alcohol` 0.24 FALSE EQUALS `no allowance` `nil under the s 24 (4) table`
-- ... at 0.30, but the person satisfied the Board the alcohol did not contribute (s 24 (4A)): the full $1 200.
#ASSERT `an employee's allowance` `continuously, for one week or more but less than 12 months, up to the day of the accident` 39000 (DATE_FROM_DMY 9 9 2025) 0 0 TRUE `section 6 (1): driving with a prescribed concentration of alcohol` 0.30 TRUE EQUALS `weekly allowance` `an employed person's allowance` 1200 1200 (DATE_FROM_DMY 17 3 2026) (DATE_FROM_DMY 6 3 2028) (DATE_FROM_DMY 3 3 2031)
-- ... at 0.03 (a novice driver's limit): the table has no row: not covered (finding 8).
#ASSERT `an employee's allowance` `continuously, for one week or more but less than 12 months, up to the day of the accident` 39000 (DATE_FROM_DMY 9 9 2025) 0 0 TRUE `section 6 (1): driving with a prescribed concentration of alcohol` 0.03 FALSE EQUALS `allowance not covered` `a conviction under s 6 (1) of the Road Safety (Alcohol and Drugs) Act 1970 below 0.05: the s 24 (4) table has no row for it`
-- s 14 (2): nil, and (4A) does not save it.
#ASSERT `an employee's allowance` `continuously, for one week or more but less than 12 months, up to the day of the accident` 39000 (DATE_FROM_DMY 9 9 2025) 0 0 TRUE `section 14 (2)` 0 TRUE EQUALS `no allowance` `nil under the s 24 (4) table`
-- cl 6 (2): not wholly disabled within the first 20 days.
#ASSERT `an employee's allowance` `continuously for the whole 12 months before the day of the accident` 73000 `the accident` 0 0 FALSE `none` 0 FALSE EQUALS `no allowance` `not wholly disabled within 20 days beginning on the day of the accident (Sch 1 Pt 5 cl 6 (2))`
-- cl 3 (6): AWE $350 (comparable worker): the lesser of $320 and $350: $320.
