    `is a full-time student` IS FALSE
    `ordinarily resided with the person at the same premises` IS TRUE
    `was principally dependent on the person for financial support` IS TRUE
    `is the parent or step-parent of a dependent child who would, but for the death, be dependent on the person for care` IS FALSE
    `was born from a pregnancy at the time of the accident` IS FALSE
    `survived the person by the cl 7 period of 30 days` IS TRUE
#ASSERT `the death benefit lump sum for the survivors` `the accident` TRUE (LIST `the spouse`, `the child of 5`, `the child of 17`) 0 EQUALS `dollars` 114000

-- Funeral benefits (Pt 3). Limit: AWE $1 000 in May 2007, $2 000 now: I% = 100%: 7 500 + 7 500 = $15 000.
#ASSERT `What is the most MAIB pays for the funeral` `the accident` 1000 2000 EQUALS `dollars` 15000
-- $1 000 to $1 800: I% = 80%: 7 500 + 6 000 = $13 500.
#ASSERT `What is the most MAIB pays for the funeral` `the accident` 1000 1800 EQUALS `dollars` 13500
-- AWE fell, $1 000 to $900: no increase: $7 500 (a reading).
#ASSERT `What is the most MAIB pays for the funeral` `the accident` 1000 900 EQUALS `dollars` 7500
-- An accident in 2005 (cl 2 (2): the 2000 Regulations): not covered.
#ASSERT `What is the most MAIB pays for the funeral` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 6 2005) 1000 2000 EQUALS `amount not covered` `funeral benefits for an accident before 1 December 2007: the 2000 Regulations apply, which are not deposited`
-- $16 000 of expenses, $3 000 of it the headstone: $13 000, under the $13 500 limit.
#ASSERT `What funeral benefit is payable` `the accident` TRUE 16000 3000 1000 1800 EQUALS `dollars` 13000
-- $20 000, $2 000 headstone: $18 000, cut to the $13 500 limit.
#ASSERT `What funeral benefit is payable` `the accident` TRUE 20000 2000 1000 1800 EQUALS `dollars` 13500
#ASSERT `What funeral benefit is payable` `the accident` FALSE 20000 2000 1000 1800 EQUALS `nothing payable` `the death did not result directly from the motor accident`

§§ `Counselling for family members (Sch 1 Pt 7)`

-- A sister of a person needing daily care; $2 000 of psychologist's fees; accident in 2026: $1 270.
#ASSERT `What counselling benefit can I get` `the accident` TRUE FALSE `a sibling` TRUE TRUE 2000 EQUALS `dollars` 1270
-- $900 of fees: $900.
#ASSERT `What counselling benefit can I get` `the accident` FALSE TRUE `a parent` TRUE TRUE 900 EQUALS `dollars` 900
-- An accident in 2015: the $1 000 limit (cl 1 (2) (a)).
#ASSERT `What counselling benefit can I get` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 6 2015) TRUE FALSE `a child` TRUE TRUE 1500 EQUALS `dollars` 1000
-- An accident in 2006: before 1 December 2007.
#ASSERT `What counselling benefit can I get` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 6 2006) TRUE FALSE `a child` TRUE TRUE 1500 EQUALS `nothing payable` `the accident occurred before 1 December 2007 (Sch 1 Pt 7 cl 1 (1) (a))`
-- The injured person neither needs daily care nor died.
#ASSERT `What counselling benefit can I get` `the accident` FALSE FALSE `a parent` TRUE TRUE 900 EQUALS `nothing payable` `neither the injured person requires daily care nor has the injured person died (Sch 1 Pt 7 cl 1 (1) (a))`
-- A cousin who does not live with them: not a family member.
#ASSERT `What counselling benefit can I get` `the accident` FALSE TRUE `another person` TRUE TRUE 900 EQUALS `nothing payable` `not a family member (s 23 (8))`
-- An aunt who lives with them: (e).
#ASSERT `What counselling benefit can I get` `the accident` FALSE TRUE `a relative or step-relative who lives with the injured person` TRUE TRUE 900 EQUALS `dollars` 900
-- A counsellor who is not a psychologist and not supervised by one.
#ASSERT `What counselling benefit can I get` `the accident` FALSE TRUE `a parent` TRUE FALSE 900 EQUALS `nothing payable` `the counselling is not provided by, or under the supervision of, a registered psychologist (s 23 (8))`

